{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb0gi2648n","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"active-claim requires native Claude task file not just overlay graph node","summary":"The orch-gate's /active-claim endpoint resolves claims through the native Claude task file layer (~/.claude/tasks/<session>/<id>.json), not just the .graph/nodes/ overlay. When subagents call start_task with a new key that was never created via TaskCreate, the overlay writes to .graph/nodes/ but the daemon's in-memory graph never sees it (no native file → task invisible). Fix: orchestrator MUST call TaskCreate (native) first to get the task ID, then pass that full key to subagents for start_task. Keys like b3d1b5f4.../32 created via TaskCreate work; keys invented by agents do not.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T14:17:28.686Z","vec":[-0.08984355628490448,0.05267683044075966,-0.029878368601202965,-0.0027441068086773157,0.12957565486431122,-0.011087989434599876,-0.00004892264405498281,0.0611148476600647,-0.047341488301754,0.10668455809354782,-0.0005884433048777282,-0.007319784723222256,-0.01804453134536743,0.04509732872247696,0.04917474463582039,0.023077500984072685,0.04299534857273102,-0.06744447350502014,0.08154059946537018,-0.03367526829242706,-0.02167426235973835,-0.06346218287944794,0.032180313020944595,0.030535701662302017,0.05581605061888695,-0.10431532561779022,-0.09149310737848282,0.020784862339496613,0.031000597402453423,-0.004396754316985607,0.06874457001686096,0.060336675494909286,0.01858675666153431,-0.016398604959249496,0.06505318731069565,0.08007633686065674,-0.07412351667881012,-0.022924546152353287,-0.09002222865819931,-0.018884848803281784,0.07378705590963364,0.05813721939921379,-0.04977769777178764,-0.004755556583404541,-0.030610164627432823,-0.0030319993384182453,-0.04049527645111084,-0.02633826434612274,-0.003966472577303648,0.0866536796092987,-0.04247045889496803,-0.04008316248655319,0.048941608518362045,-0.12082754075527191,0.003318777307868004,0.032195